in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @magic
in @kintsugi
in @epistemologic
in @epistemologic/property
in @mirror

# @mirror/docs — the substrate-decl form of docs/ taxonomy. The
# substrate describes itself in substrate the same way mirror
# describes itself in mirror.
#
# Recognition #90 candidate (Alex 2026-06-20; landed in the same
# session that recognized #85→#89 closing the cascade). The substrate-
# honest collision shape Alex named across today's cascade recurs at
# the documentation altitude: docs/ ⇔ @mirror/docs (cleanup-as-
# operator vs docs-as-substrate-decl). Same #pack-G2 pattern as
# /loop ⇔ @loop (#88); @reflection-family ⇔ @reflection/reflection-
# Model; reference ⇔ reflection (#89); reed-as-relationship ⇔
# reed-as-peer.
#
# Tick 45 of the refined /loop discipline / tick 1 of the docs/
# ouroboros loop. Per Reed-as-substrate-actor cleanup audit
# (2026-06-20 cleanup-review): 18 top-level files audited (13
# SUPERSEDED archive candidates, 4 CURRENT, 1 HONEST_HISTORY); 13
# subdirectories; ~195 files total. The audit surfaced THREE
# organizational findings that this family-root makes substrate-
# fact: (S-1) top-level convention undefined; (S-3) audits/+
# reviews/+review/ are three names for one job; (S-4) dating
# discipline varies by kind.
#
# === The recognition ===
#
# The substrate had every primitive for self-describing docs:
# - prism (the typed-record algebra for taxonomy)
# - glass (the imperfect/transparency carrier for classification)
# - kintsugi (the loop that moves docs into right shape)
# - pact + fracture (the bilateral pattern for "classify + repair")
# - splinter(ast) (the AST-altitude move-shard morphisms)
#
# What was missing: the family-root that NAMES the docs taxonomy as
# substrate. This shard is that name. After it lands, the kintsugi
# loop can drive docs/ cleanup substrate-pull-correctly: each tick
# applies one morphism (move file, consolidate subdir, archive
# superseded); dark_count decreases monotonically; the substrate
# witnesses its own cleanup.
#
# === The taxonomy_kind variant ===
#
# Per Seam C4 closure pattern (variants over bare ref-with-documented-
# values): typed substrate variant naming the docs subdirectory kinds.
# Same-shape different-meaning forbidden per [[feedback-no-bare-
# types]].
#
# The kinds surveyed in the cleanup audit:
# - spec: substrate-decl specifications (evergreen; lives at docs/specs/)
# - insight: dated synthesis documents (lives at docs/insights/)
# - audit: adversarial-review records (dated; Seam-authored typically)
# - research: long-form research synthesis (lives at docs/research/)
# - plan: planning documents (lives at docs/plans/; mostly superseded)
# - roadmap: phased work tracks (lives at docs/roadmap/)
# - math: mathematical-altitude documentation (lives at docs/math/)
# - cicd: CI/CD operational docs (lives at docs/cicd/)
# - ai: AI-specific architectural docs (lives at docs/ai/)
# - hook: git/build hook documentation (lives at docs/hooks/)
# - benchmark: benchmark notes (lives at docs/benchmarks/)
# - cleanup_review: dated self-cleanup audits (lives at docs/ top-
#   level; HONEST_HISTORY convention)
# - grant: grant/funding artifacts (lives at docs/ top-level)
# - ops: operational notes (CACHE.md, root-focus.md, etc.; docs/ top-
#   level)
# - branding: brand/visual artifacts (logo-prompt.md, etc.; docs/
#   top-level)
# - archive: superseded docs preserved as honest-history (lives at
#   docs/archive/<original-path>; substrate-pull-correct convention)
# - unknown: forward-promised refinement for [UNSURE] register
#
# === The dating_discipline variant ===
#
# Per S-4 cleanup audit finding: dating varies by kind. This variant
# names the substrate's canonical conventions:
# - evergreen: spec docs (substrate-decl specifications; rewritten in
#   place; no date in filename)
# - dated: insight + audit + cleanup_review (snapshot at a tick;
#   filename carries YYYY-MM-DD prefix)
# - date_suffixed_on_respec: per-recognition canonical specs
#   (filename adds a date suffix when re-spec'd; preserves prior
#   versions implicitly)
# - undated: ops/branding/grant (no date convention; rewritten in
#   place)
#
# === The supersession_status variant ===
#
# Per Reed-agent cleanup categories: classification of each doc's
# relationship to current substrate.
# - current: actively referenced by landed substrate (#80→#89 shards);
#   keep
# - superseded: described a recognition or design that landed
#   substrate-decl shards replaced; archive candidate
# - stale: old enough AND not referenced; review candidate
# - orphan: at wrong path (top-level should be in subdir); move
#   candidate
# - duplicate: two docs describing the same thing; consolidate
#   candidate
# - contradictory: describes substrate state contradicting current
#   shards; rewrite or delete candidate
# - honest_history: stale but preserved as historical record
#   (cleanup-review-2026-04-29.md is the prior example); keep with
#   note
#
# === The archive convention ===
#
# Per the cleanup audit's structural finding: superseded docs do NOT
# get deleted (no-add-without-pact + no-delete-without-pact). They
# move to docs/archive/<original-path> with a supersession header
# explaining WHY they're archived and WHAT they're superseded by.
# This preserves the substrate's honest-history discipline; the
# move is content-addressed (git history retains the original path);
# the archive is the substrate's own past.
#
# === Composes with the cascade ===
#
# - @mirror/ref (#89): docs/ cleanup pipelines ARE @mirror/ref queries
#   (`mirror ref where 'taxonomy_kind = superseded' | settle
#   archive_doc`); the navigation surface drives the docs-cleanup
#   ouroboros loop
# - @loop (#88): each docs cleanup tick IS one @loop iteration at the
#   docs-discipline altitude; loop_well_founded cascades
# - @mirror/bench (#87): each doc classification persists as a bench
#   crystal at the docs altitude (forward-promised dispatch)
# - @loop (#86; @moi absorbed 2026-07-01 Loki §1): doc_record
#   records are moi(doc_record) at composition time (pact-verified
#   that the classification respects the taxonomy)
# - @kintsugi: the cleanup ouroboros loop IS @kintsugi at the docs
#   altitude
# - @magic family: the substrate's mechanism+contract+audit+reveal
#   discipline at substrate-decl altitude maps to docs/ at the
#   documentation altitude
# - @epistemologic/property/* + @kintsugi/fracture/* (#53 bilateral):
#   each docs cleanup discipline becomes a property+fracture pair
#   (forward-promised; tick 2+ of this loop)
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   Knuth literate programming   1984; tangled source + woven docs;
#                                the substrate's content-addressed
#                                substrate-decl IS literate
#                                programming at type-system altitude.
#   Diataxis framework           Procida 2017+; tutorials/how-to/
#                                reference/explanation as four kinds
#                                of documentation. The substrate's
#                                taxonomy_kind variant lifts this
#                                discipline at substrate-decl
#                                altitude.
#   Maven/Gradle conventions     directory layout as convention
#                                (src/main vs src/test vs docs); the
#                                substrate's subdir-per-kind echoes
#                                this at documentation altitude.
#   Rust's docs.rs              autogenerated rustdoc; convention-
#                                over-configuration for docs. The
#                                substrate gets this for free via
#                                content-addressed substrate-decl.
#   Wikipedia categorization     hierarchical kind + cross-reference;
#                                the substrate's @mirror/docs and
#                                @mirror/ref compose to give the
#                                same discipline at substrate-decl
#                                altitude.
#
# Spec context: docs/cleanup-review-2026-06-20.md (Reed-agent cleanup
#               audit grounding this tick; 18 top-level + 13 subdirs
#               + ~195 files).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-mirror-ref-reference-reflection-
#                       collision]] (#89; the navigation surface that
#                       drives docs cleanup),
#                      [[architecture-loop-as-monad]] (#88; each
#                       cleanup tick IS one @loop iteration),
#                      [[architecture-mirror-bench-ouroboros]] (#87;
#                       bench measures docs cleanup runtime),
#                      [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-alignment-as-boundary-
#                       mathematics]] (#57; doc_well_classified IS the
#                       boundary-harness at documentation altitude),
#                      [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]
#                       (56th+ instance; the substrate had every
#                       primitive for self-describing docs).
# Related shards: mirror/ref.mirror (the navigation surface; docs
#                  cleanup uses ref to find and move docs),
#                 mirror/bench.mirror (perf measurement of cleanup
#                  iterations),
#                 loop.mirror (the iterative discipline this loop
#                  inherits),
#                 moi.mirror (the monad family-root; doc_record
#                  results pass through moi at composition).
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/mirror/docs.mirror`
# declares `@mirror/docs` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/programming/knuth-1984
source @arxiv/documentation/procida-2017

prism @mirror/docs {
  focus  docs
  project docs
  split  docs
  shift  docs
  settle docs
}

# === The taxonomy_kind variant ===
#
# Per Seam C4 closure pattern: typed substrate variant naming the
# canonical docs subdirectory kinds. Each kind discriminates the
# downstream subdir + dating discipline + lifecycle convention.
type taxonomy_kind =
  | spec
  | insight
  | audit
  | research
  | plan
  | roadmap
  | math
  | cicd
  | ai
  | hook
  | benchmark
  | cleanup_review
  | grant
  | ops
  | branding
  | archive
  | unknown

# === The dating_discipline variant ===
#
# Per S-4 cleanup audit finding: dating varies by kind. The substrate
# names the four canonical conventions.
type dating_discipline =
  | evergreen
  | dated
  | date_suffixed_on_respec
  | undated

# === The supersession_status variant ===
#
# Per Reed-agent cleanup categories: classification of each doc's
# relationship to current substrate. Bilateral predicate
# doc_well_classified discriminates on this variant.
type supersession_status =
  | current
  | superseded
  | stale
  | orphan
  | duplicate
  | contradictory
  | honest_history

# === The archive_location carrier ===
#
# Typed reference for the archive destination of a superseded doc.
# Per the archive convention: docs/archive/<original-path>.
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type archive_location = ref

# === The doc_record carrier ===
#
# Per [[feedback-no-bare-types]]: typed record over (path,
# taxonomy_kind, dating_discipline, supersession_status). The
# substrate-architectural object @mirror/docs instances are records
# over typed family carriers, not bare refs.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the quadruple.
type doc_record = {
  path:       ref,
  kind:       taxonomy_kind,
  dating:     dating_discipline,
  status:     supersession_status,
}

# === classify action ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING ACTION at @mirror/docs altitude. Given a doc
# path, returns the typed doc_record carrying its taxonomy
# classification + dating + supersession status.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary; the classification
# heuristic reads the path (subdirectory + filename), the file
# content (header), and cross-references against landed shards on
# main to discriminate current vs superseded.
classify(path: ref) -> doc_record { \ }

# === subdir_for action ===
#
# Returns the canonical subdir for a taxonomy kind. The substrate's
# convention-over-configuration discipline at documentation altitude.
subdir_for(k: taxonomy_kind) -> ref { \ }

# === archive action (FIRST non-decorative consumer of
# doc_well_classified) ===
#
# Moves a superseded doc to its archive location per the archive
# convention. The substrate-pull-correct equivalent of "preserve as
# honest-history; don't delete."
#
# requires doc_well_classified(d): the substrate forecloses
# archiving misclassified docs. Without this requires clause,
# archive would admit incorrect moves (the @magic tick-11 dead-
# letter pattern at docs altitude). The bilateral predicate IS the
# substrate's archive-correctness check.
#
# Body discharges via the @kintsugi loop's morphism application;
# the actual move is implemented by the realisation boundary's git
# mv (preserving content-addressed history).
archive(d: doc_record) -> archive_location
requires doc_well_classified(d)
{ \ }

# === consolidate action ===
#
# Consolidates multiple subdirectory names for the same taxonomy_kind
# (per S-3 cleanup finding: audits/ + reviews/ + review/ are three
# names for one job). Returns the canonical subdir; the realisation
# layer moves files from the redundant subdirs into the canonical
# one.
consolidate(redundant: ref, canonical: ref, k: taxonomy_kind) -> ref { \ }

# === doc_well_classified predicate (bilateral) ===
#
# Bilateral verdict per recognition #37 (Pask agreement) AND the
# alignment-as-boundary-mathematics check (#57) at documentation
# altitude. Returns verdict that a doc_record's classification is
# substrate-architecturally well-formed:
# - path matches the subdir for kind
# - dating discipline matches kind's convention
# - supersession status is current evidence-grounded (per cross-
#   reference against landed substrate)
#
# Per Seam B1 closure pattern: archive (above) is the FIRST non-
# decorative consumer via `requires doc_well_classified(d)`.
#
# Discharge: substrate-pull-correct classification check at the
# species boundary. Bounded → doc is substrate-architecturally well-
# classified (admit archive); unbounded → doc violates one or more
# substrate-pull constraints (archive refused; manual review
# required).
#
# Same shape as the bilateral predicates the prior family-roots
# carry:
# - @magic: invariant_preserved, audited, mechanism_intact
# - @frame: bounded_commutator_check
# - @smarts: discipline_flexible
# - @cyberpunk: cybernetic_coherence
# - @pack: pack_coherent
# - @pack/seam: review_sound
# - @loop: pact_respected (absorbed from @moi 2026-07-01)
# - @reflection: loss_decreases, speaks_at_n_plus_1
# - @smarts/reflection: bridge_coherent
# - @reflection/surface: translation_faithful
# - @reflection/mirror: path_coherent
# - @mirror/bench: monotone_non_increasing, bench_overhead_below_floor
# - @loop: loop_well_founded
# - @mirror/store/crystal: crystal_well_formed
# - @mirror/ref: ref_query_compositional, interface_authored_by_human
# - @mirror/docs: doc_well_classified (this one)
doc_well_classified(d: doc_record) -> verdict { \ }

out @mirror/docs
out taxonomy_kind
out dating_discipline
out supersession_status
out archive_location
out doc_record
out classify
out subdir_for
out archive
out consolidate
out doc_well_classified
